    kind: work_item  # 744e
    title: "Go interface satisfaction must traverse promoted methods from embedded types"  # 744e
    status: todo_soft  # 744e
    priority: 3  # 744e
    parent:  # 744e
    tags:  # 744e
    - go  # 744e
    - analysis_quality  # 744e
    - cross_language_linkers  # 744e
    before: []  # 744e
    duplicate_of: []  # 744e
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 744e
    pr_ref:  # 744e
    description: "Discovered while investigating WI-sukav. The Go structural interface matcher creates 'implements' edges only when a type explicitly defines all required methods, but doesn't account for methods promoted via embedding. Confirmed in alertmanager timeinterval.go: the type \\`stringableRange\\` interface requires setBegin, setEnd, memberFromString. InclusiveRange explicitly defines all three and gets implements: InclusiveRange → stringableRange (correct). WeekdayRange embeds InclusiveRange (so it inherits setBegin/setEnd via promotion) and explicitly defines its own memberFromString — meaning *WeekdayRange satisfies stringableRange. But hg.json shows NO implements edge from WeekdayRange to stringableRange. Same gap for DayOfMonthRange, MonthRange, YearRange. The structural matcher needs to traverse the type's embedding chain when checking interface satisfaction. Fix should also update find_implementing_methods in type_hierarchy.py to include embedder types as implementers when their explicit methods + their embedded types' methods cover the interface."  # 744e
    fields: {}  # 744e
